From 8ac7867b329204477a47dfe4cdf0e32abc4275ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shixuantong <sxt1001@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:31:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Validate raid tool output before building shell commands in
 bmc_ras_sentry

storcli64/hiraidadm output is parsed into ctrlId/VDId/encId/slotId/VDName
fields, re-assembled into commands via format_string, and executed through
popen() as root - a maliciously crafted tool output (compromised tool
binary, hijacked firmware, or tampered enclosure data) could inject
arbitrary shell commands.

- add IsValidSafeToken(): whitelist of alphanumerics plus : / - _ (no
  shell metacharacters); empty string, NA and N/A placeholders are also
  accepted
- validate every tainted field at each command construction site and at
  the parsing sources (VD LIST, EID:Slt, Enc/Slot columns), rejecting
  unsafe values with a warning log
- guard SplitString().back() on an empty result for the VD name in both
  storcli and hiraidadm paths: an empty "OS Drive Name" field would hit
  undefined behavior on an empty vector and crash the root daemon before
  the token check could run

hiraidadm ctrlId/VDId values are int-typed through json_type_int checks
and formatted with %d, so they cannot carry injection payloads and need
no token validation.

Co-Authored-By: GLM-5.3
